        <div class="row gy-5 gx-lg-5">
            <main class="col-lg-8">
                <p class="lead-copy">Company law and LLP compliance is an ongoing responsibility involving directors, shareholders, statutory records, meetings, filings and regulatory reporting. Sonagra &amp; Company helps businesses manage these requirements with clear documentation, timely action and practical corporate guidance.</p>
                <p>Our support covers routine compliance as well as structural changes, certifications, audits, regulatory searches and representation before the Registrar of Companies and other authorities.</p>

                <div class="company-law-reference-list">
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>01</span><p>All matters connected with Company Law, Rules and Regulations including Board of Directors Compliances, Shareholders Compliances, Charge Registration and Rectification, Search and Status Reports, and all other compliances.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>02</span><p>Corporatization of Partnerships and Sole Proprietary Firms.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>03</span><p>Conversion of existing companies, partnerships and sole-proprietary firms into LLPs in a cost and tax-efficient manner, subject to applicable legal requirements.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>04</span><p>Advisory and compliances pertaining to Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR).</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>05</span><p>Setting up, obtaining licenses, renewals and carrying out compliances for Banking Companies and Non-Banking Financial Companies, including Asset Finance Companies, Micro Finance Institutions and Core Investment Companies.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>06</span><p>Drafting of Board policies under the Companies Act, 2013, Listing Regulations, Non-Banking Financial Companies Regulations and other applicable frameworks.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>07</span><p>Drafting documentation in respect of Board and General Meetings.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>08</span><p>Preparation and certification of various statutory forms.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>09</span><p>Issuance of Annual Return Certificate (MGT.8).</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>10</span><p>Preparation of Directors’ Report.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>11</span><p>Updating Statutory Records and Registers.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>12</span><p>Attending the Board and General Meetings.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>13</span><p>Issuance of Secretarial Audit Report.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>14</span><p>Internal Audit.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>15</span><p>Audit and Certifications under Listing Regulations and other Capital Market Regulations.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>16</span><p>Name Change, Object Change and shifting of Registered Office.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>17</span><p>Providing Bank Due Diligence Certificate.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>18</span><p>Physical Search from ROCs and Documents Obtention.</p></div>
                    <div class="company-law-reference-item"><span>19</span><p>Appearing before the Regional Director and Registrar of Companies.</p></div>
                </div>
